  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements, one is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R.</p><p>Assertion A : Order of acidic nature of the following compounds is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8b20b1d1-6e92-4f6b-9094-d43346c66690.png\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 152px;\" /></p><p>Reason R: Fluoro is a stronger electron withdrawing group than Chloro group.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "66lb0",
      "text": "A is false but R is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NVIVX",
      "text": "Both A and R are correct and R is the correct explanation of A",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rydFZ",
      "text": "A is true but R is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "o680h",
      "text": "Both A and R are correct but R is NOT the correct explanation of A",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The electron withdrawing groups decreases the acidic nature and&nbsp;The electron releasing&nbsp;groups increases the acidic nature.</p><p>The<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math> are electron withdrawing while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is electron loosing hence acidic strength will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8555480f-a48a-4a05-9c68-c541e6b6d237.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 157px;\" /></p><p>On further differentiation the<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> effect depends on most importantly over distance hence.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6b80bb87-d954-4e77-9a43-81562a1dd606.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 161px;\" /></p><p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>&nbsp;has higher <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> effect as compared to Cl hence reason is correct statement but the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> effect depends more on distance as compared to power&nbsp;hence&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c9d05d5a-0564-4cf3-9979-38bd04fc88c7.png\" style=\"width: 100px; height: 115px;\" />&nbsp;is stronger acid than&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8bf607cb-e706-4d69-8b91-8cd09560c8b9.png\" style=\"width: 80px; height: 175px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
